meta {
  name: 06b Export Aufgaben (JSON container)
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/hellodata/v1/json/aufgaben
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

tests {
  test("response is JSON", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    expect(res.getHeader("content-type")).to.contain("application/json");
  });

  test("container object holds the rows in a data array", function() {
    const body = res.getBody();

    expect(body).to.be.an("object");
    expect(body.data).to.be.an("array");
  });

  test("_meta closes the document and its rowCount matches", function() {
    // Without _meta the response was truncated and the load counts as failed -
    // after HTTP 200 no error can be reported any more. Note that _meta is the
    // LAST member: rowCount is only known once the last row has been streamed.
    const body = res.getBody();

    expect(body._meta).to.not.equal(undefined);
    expect(body._meta.status).to.equal("complete");
    expect(body._meta.rowCount).to.equal(body.data.length);
  });
}

docs {
  Same data as `06a Export Aufgaben (NDJSON)`, framed as one ordinary JSON document
  for consumers that cannot ingest NDJSON:

      {"data":[ {...}, {...} ],"_meta":{"status":"complete","rowCount":2,...}}

  Each row carries the Aufgabe id, the AufgabeStatus, the Faelligkeitsdatum
  (`faelligBis`), the foreign keys to the erfassender (`userErfasst`) and the
  verantwortlicher Benutzer (`empfaenger`), the optional foreign keys to Kind
  (`kindId`) and Anlass (`anlassId`) and the assigned Labels as a comma-separated
  list of Label UUIDs. Titel, Bemerkung, the file attachments and the Link are never
  exported (free text / internal deep link, may contain personal data).

  Aufgaben are not tenant-scoped in the database, but the BE-only access gate applies,
  so `baseUrl` must point at the BE host.

  The server streams this exactly like the NDJSON variant (the braces, commas and
  the trailing `_meta` are written as the rows come off the cursor). What changes
  is the client side: `JSON.parse` / `json.loads` has to buffer the whole document
  before it sees the first row. That is why NDJSON stays the recommended format.

  Checking that the server really streams (Bruno buffers the response, hence curl):

      curl -N -w '\nstart=%{time_starttransfer}s total=%{time_total}s\n' \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
        -H "Accept: application/json" \
        https://local-esc-be.localhost:6443/api/hellodata/v1/json/aufgaben

  If `time_starttransfer` is well below `time_total`, the cursor is live.
}
